	(text "Every multimeter output is read through 100k (series) into a 74HCT165 input, with a\n100k pull-down on the connector side:\n - TTL-compatible thresholds for the 7404 outputs of the 70754 unit\n - < 35 uA per line into the input clamp diodes when the isolated supply is off\n   (USB unplugged), so the multimeter cannot back-power this board\n - defined (all-zero) data when the board is not plugged into the multimeter\n\nSerial stream at MISO after a LATCH pulse (first bit first):\n  bit 0..35  = SKB pin 1..36  (bit n = pin n+1)\n  bit 36     = SKB pin 38 read-back (FRONT PANEL LOCKOUT line; high = DVM powered)\n  bit 37..39 = 1,0,0  hard-wired marker (checks chain length / isolated supply present)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240 196 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4 1.4)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d88695ac-b00a-5c3c-9991-40332f781ef4")
	)
	(text "100k pull-downs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.64 111.5 0)
